  <!-- ──────────────── DAY HIKES / TRIPS AND WALKS ──────────────── -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">Day Hikes / Trips and Walks</div>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Doi Suthep Monk's Trail</strong> — 5 km return, moderate, no guide required, free. A shaded forest walk leading up to Wat Pha Lat and on to Doi Suthep.</li>
      <li><strong>Doi Inthanon National Park trails</strong> — short walks from 2–6 km, easy to moderate, no guide required. Park entry around 300 THB. Thailand's highest peak is here and temperatures can feel surprisingly cold early in the morning.</li>
      <li><strong>Kew Mae Pan Nature Trail</strong> — roughly 3 km loop, moderate, local guide required during open season. Guide fee around 200 THB per group.</li>
      <li><strong>Pai</strong> — ~3 hours north by minivan (~150–200 THB each way). Pai Canyon is a 1 km ridge walk with optional scrambling, plus hot springs, waterfalls, and riverside cafes. Most travellers stay 2–3 nights rather than day-trip it.</li>
      <li><strong>Chiang Dao</strong> — ~1.5 hours north by minivan (~80–120 THB each way). Tham Chiang Dao is a guided ~1 km lamp-lit cave walk (~40 THB entry, ~100 THB lamp guide). Karst mountain and forest trails outside town for fitter visitors.</li>
      <li><strong>Lampang</strong> — ~1.5 hours south by train (~50 THB). Walkable Lanna old town, wooden shophouses, horse-drawn carriages, and Wat Phra That Lampang Luang ~20 km out. Suits a slow cultural day trip.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

